turns.content:
Here’s a reusable weekly email template that stays skimmable, works when some metrics are missing, and makes “asks/decisions” impossible to ignore. It’s designed so you can fill it in fast and still send even if data isn’t ready.

---

## Subject line options (pick one and standardize)
1) **[Prod+Ops Weekly] Metrics + Highlights — Week ending {DATE}**  
2) **Weekly Scorecard ({DATE}) — Wins, Risks, Asks**  
3) **{TEAM} Weekly: What changed + what we need ({DATE})**

---

## Email template (copy/paste)

**[Prod+Ops Weekly] — Week ending {DATE}**  
Owner: {NAME} | Data as of: {TIMESTAMP} | Links: {Dashboard} {Jira/Linear} {Incident log}

---

### 1) TL;DR (read this if nothing else)
- **Win:** {one line}
- **Risk/Issue:** {one line}
- **What changed most:** {one line} (ex: “Signups +12% WoW due to X”)

---

### 2) Scorecard (key metrics)
*(If a metric is missing, write “TBD (expected {when})” — don’t leave blanks.)*

| Metric | This week | WoW | Target | Note |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
| {Metric 1} | {# / TBD} | {+/- %} | {#} | {1 short why} |
| {Metric 2} | {# / TBD} | {+/- %} | {#} | {1 short why} |
| {Metric 3} | {# / TBD} | {+/- %} | {#} | {1 short why} |
| {Metric 4} | {# / TBD} | {+/- %} | {#} | {1 short why} |

**Data gaps:** {none / list what’s missing + when it’ll be updated}

---

### 3) What shipped / progressed (by area)
- **Product:** {1–3 bullets max}
- **Ops:** {1–3 bullets max}
- **Eng/Data (if relevant):** {1–3 bullets max}

---

### 4) Asks / decisions needed (reply requested)
*(Keep this near the top; each item should be answerable in one sentence.)*

1) **Decision needed:** {A vs B} — **by {DATE}**  
   - Context: {1 line}  
   - Recommendation: {1 line}

2) **Approval needed:** {budget/headcount/tool/etc} — **by {DATE}**  
   - Impact if delayed: {1 line}

3) **Help needed:** {intro/unblocker/etc} — **by {DATE}**  
   - Owner: {name}

---

### 5) Risks / watchlist (not blocking yet)
- {Risk} — likelihood {L/M/H}, impact {L/M/H}, mitigation {1 line}, owner {name}
- {Risk}

---

### 6) Next week focus (top 3)
1) {#1}
2) {#2}
3) {#3}

---

### 7) FYI (optional, keep short)
- {Upcoming milestone/date}
- {Customer/partner note}
- {Link to deeper write-up}

---

## Quick rules that keep it readable
- **Max 1 screen before scrolling** (everything else goes in links).
- **3 bullets max per section** unless it’s the scorecard.
- Always include **“reply requested by DATE”** in Asks.

---

If you tell me 1) the **4–6 metrics** you care about most, and 2) whether your audience is mostly **execs vs ICs**, I can tailor the scorecard columns (WoW vs MoM, targets, segment breakdowns) so it matches how your org actually reviews performance.

