One more “heads up” so you don’t get confused on the **email vs History**: your email WoW rendering uses `wowCell()` and prints `12.3%` by doing `toFixed(1)` on the raw percent value. The History now stores WoW as a fraction. That’s fine because they’re separate paths, but if later you reuse the History values anywhere, remember they’re fractions.

If you want to make it impossible to mix them up, you can standardize on “fraction everywhere” by changing `pctChange_()` to return a fraction instead of percent:

```js
function pctChange_(cur, prev) {
  if (!prev) return null;
  return (cur - prev) / prev; // fraction, e.g. 0.123
}
```

Then update your email formatter to multiply by 100:

```js
const wowCell = (v) => {
  if (v === null || v === undefined) return "N/A";
  const pct = v * 100;
  const arrow = pct >= 0 ? "▲" : "▼";
  return `${arrow} ${Math.abs(pct).toFixed(1)}%`;
};
```

And you’d remove the `/ 100` in `logRun_()` since it would already be a fraction.

Not required, but it keeps one convention across the whole script and avoids future mistakes. Want me to give you the exact 3-line edits to switch to “fraction everywhere”?

