Awesome! You’re now **fully decoupling the HTTP and HTTPS flows** while still keeping `/health` **accessible via HTTP without redirection or authentication** — a clean and safe pattern for container health checks and monitoring tools.

Let me summarize and refine the final setup you're working with, and offer a **ready-to-use version** with **additional optional tweaks** for monitoring and security.

---

## ✅ Final Nginx Config (`nginx/nginx.conf`)

```nginx
events {}

upstream dashboard_app {
    server app:8000;
}

http {
    server {
        listen 80;
        server_name localhost;

        # HTTP health endpoint — no redirect, no auth
        location = /health {
            proxy_pass http://dashboard_app/health;
            proxy_set_header Host $host;
            proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
            proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        }

        # Redirect all other HTTP traffic to HTTPS
        location / {
            return 301 https://$host$request_uri;
        }
    }

    server {
        listen 443 ssl;
        server_name localhost;

        ssl_certificate     /etc/nginx/certs/dashboard.crt;
        ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/certs/dashboard.key;

        # All HTTPS traffic is proxied to FastAPI
        location / {
            proxy_pass http://dashboard_app;
            proxy_set_header Host $host;
            proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
            proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        }
    }
}
```

---

## ✅ Behavior Summary

| URL | Protocol | Auth | Description |
|-----|----------|------|-------------|
| `http://localhost/health` | HTTP | No | FastAPI health endpoint, no redirect or auth |
| `http://localhost/` | HTTP | No | Redirects to HTTPS |
| `https://localhost/health` | HTTPS | No | Optional (not needed if HTTP is already open) |
| `https://localhost/` | HTTPS | Yes | Dashboard (protected by Basic Auth) |
| `https://localhost/api/metrics` | HTTPS | Yes | API (protected by Basic Auth) |

---

## 🔧 Optional: Make `/health` also available via HTTPS

If you want **both `http://localhost/health` and `https://localhost/health`** to be available without auth, just add this to the HTTPS server block:

```nginx
    # Optional: make /health available via HTTPS as well, without redirect
    location = /health {
        proxy_pass http://dashboard_app/health;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    }
```

---

