turns.content:
Let’s do **formatted markdown rendering** but keep it safe and still “no build step”. Easiest is **markdown-it** (parser) + **DOMPurify** (sanitizer) from CDN, then render into a `<div>` instead of a `<pre>`.

### 1) Update `web/index.html`

Replace the `<pre id="markdown" ...>` with a container div:

```html
<div id="content" class="content-html"></div>
```

And add the CDN scripts *before* `app.js`:

```html
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/markdown-it@14.1.0/dist/markdown-it.min.js"></script>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/dompurify@3.1.6/dist/purify.min.js"></script>
<script src="/app.js"></script>
```

So your `<main>` section becomes (only the relevant part):

```html
<main class="content">
  <article>
    <h2 id="title"></h2>
    <div id="meta" class="meta"></div>
    <div id="content" class="content-html"></div>
  </article>
</main>
```

### 2) Update `web/app.js`

Swap the note rendering to parse + sanitize:

```js
const md = window.markdownit({
  html: false,        // don't allow raw HTML in markdown
  linkify: true,
  breaks: false
});

function renderNote(note) {
  $("title").textContent = note.title;
  $("meta").textContent = `${note.date} • ${note.slug}`;

  const unsafeHtml = md.render(note.markdown || "");
  const safeHtml = DOMPurify.sanitize(unsafeHtml);

  $("content").innerHTML = safeHtml;
  setActive(note.slug);
}
```

And remove references to `$("markdown")` since that element is gone.

### 3) Add a little CSS for nicer markdown

In `web/style.css`, add:

```css
.content-html h1, .content-html h2, .content-html h3 { margin: 16px 0 8px; }
.content-html p { line-height: 1.5; }
.content-html code { background: #f3f3f3; padding: 2px 4px; border-radius: 4px; }
.content-html pre code { display: block; padding: 12px; overflow: auto; }
.content-html a { color: #0b66c3; }
.content-html ul { padding-left: 20px; }
```

### Security posture (quick + practical)
- `markdown-it` with `html: false` means any raw `<script>` typed into a note won’t be interpreted as HTML.
- `DOMPurify` is a second layer in case links / generated HTML contain something sketchy.

### One decision I need
Do you want links in notes to open in a new tab? If yes, we can post-process rendered HTML to add `target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"` to all `<a>` tags (still safe).

